# =============================================================================
# MBC Database Backup - file-database inventory
# Spec: MBC-SPEC-BACKUP-001 v0.2, section 5.1, file-database site type
#
# Deploy as /opt/mbc-backup/sites-files.conf  --  chmod 600, chown root:root
#
# Format: sitename|engine|path
#
# - sitename is the backup key, exactly as in sites.conf. It names the files
#   and the SharePoint folder, so it must be unique across BOTH files and must
#   never change once a site has been backed up: renaming splits the history.
# - engine is currently only `sqlite`. The field exists so a second file-based
#   engine can be added without touching the format again.
# - path is the absolute path to the live database file ON THE HOST. For a
#   container using a bind mount, this is the host side of the mount, not the
#   path inside the container.
# - Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# These databases are read through the SQLite online backup API with a
# read-only connection. Nothing is written, no container is stopped, and the
# application does not need to know it is being backed up.
#
# Finding the host path of a bind-mounted database:
#   docker inspect <container> --format '{{json .Mounts}}' | python3 -m json.tool
#   -> take "Source" of the entry whose "Type" is "bind"
# =============================================================================

# max-biocare-ai stack, named Docker volumes (host path under /var/lib/docker).
max_biocare_ai_webui|sqlite|/var/lib/docker/volumes/max-biocare-ai_open-webui-data/_data/webui.db
max_biocare_ai_grafana|sqlite|/var/lib/docker/volumes/max-biocare-ai_grafana-data/_data/grafana.db
